     <widget class="QPushButton" name="run_search">
      <property name="geometry">
       <rect>
        <x>11</x>
        <y>87</y>
        <width>156</width>
        <height>26</height>
       </rect>
      </property>
      <property name="toolTip">
       <string>Ask for the files of the product over the region in the period and draw the swaths of their passes (on an empty window, over a map with coastlines made for them). Passes that do not really cross the region (NASA's search returns every pass over the antimeridian for any region) are left out, using the orbit's fixed ground tracks. A new search replaces the previous swaths.</string>
      </property>
      <property name="text">
       <string>Find the passes</string>
      </property>
      <property name="busy" stdset="0">
       <string>Finding the SWOT passes over the region…</string>
      </property>
     </widget>
     <widget class="QPushButton" name="pickline_pickpass">
      <property name="geometry">
       <rect>
        <x>178</x>
        <y>87</y>
        <width>156</width>
        <height>26</height>
       </rect>
      </property>
      <property name="toolTip">
       <string>Then click one of the swaths Find the passes drew: that pass is downloaded (if not on disk yet) and shown, as Download and show does (the oldest of its files when the period holds several cycles; the Pass list has the others). Press again to cancel. The swath's own menu item "Show this pass (SWOT)" does the same.</string>
      </property>
      <property name="text">
       <string>Pick a pass</string>
      </property>
      <property name="busy" stdset="0">
       <string>Selecting the pass…</string>
      </property>
     </widget>
    </widget>
